unbelievable...

Playing a vampiric wizard in slashem, and everything was going well. I
started out with a ring of Slow Digestion, so I had all the benefits
of vampirism (flying, regeneration, bloodsucking attack) without the
usual penalty of constantly hurrying through the levels in search of
fresh blood.

I had an unremarkable but successful first few levels, saving all my
unblessed and unID'd items for the minetown altara. It turned out to
be co-aligned, I had ID'd plenty of stuff, bought a BoH, had found
some good spells and scrolls, reached a decent xplevel and so I felt
that things were going well. Best game I've had in ages. There was
also a magic lamp (or at least a lamp worth >1000 zorkids) in the
lighting shop. However I've had a few nasty vampiric experiences with
watch captains and their silver sabers so I decided to leave the lamp
for now and steal it on the way back up.

I descended a few levels and encountered a wood nymph, who went
straight for my +ofSD! Aagh! I went off in pursuit but she found me
first and stole something else before I even saw her. I decided there
was no way i could catch her without a light source, so I duly headed
back up to minetown to get something from the shop.

On the way I stumbled onto one of my old bones piles. Loads of gold,
some interesting looking boots and gloves, stacks of rings, scrolls,
wands, gems and potions. Great! I'm heading back to minetown anyway, I
have no ?ofID left but I can at least bless some water and a scroll of
remove curse and scrub all this stuff. I cram it all into my BoH and
go straight back up to the minetown temple. Since losing my ring of SD
I'm paranoid about starving and so I'm eating (drinkning, rather)
everything I kill. Therefore when a leprechaun nabs my gold I'm more
than happy to hunt him down and bleed him dry. "You feel jumpy". Oh
well, that might come in handy, I've a feeling one of these bones
rings might be TC anyway.

So I uncurse everything (including a pair of speed boots, I'm thinking
the RNG loves me today) and I'm heading back down into the mines when
i remember the whole reason for coming here in the first place:
Getting some light to deal with that wretched nymph and retrieve my
+oSD, so I turn round and go back to the shop. I pick up a lantern (16
zorkmids) and am just considering some candles as well when the
teleportitis kicks in. "An alarm sounds", yadda yadda yadda.

I'm not panicked though, even though I just happened to teleport next
to the watch Captain, who strips off half my HP in one turn with his
silver saber. I got speed boots and teleportitis, surely I can outrun
him. I legged it out the room and wizlocked the door behind me. All I
have to do is make it to the exit, get my ring back, power up a little
between here and minesend then come back and turn this wretched
gnomeburg into a ghost town.
Except the RNG didn't love me after all. Teleportitis zapped me back
to the exact spot it had before, right next to that bloody watch
captain. Hack, chop, dywypi. *sigh*

I guess eating the leprechaun was my critical mistake, or more likely
not #chatting to find out the price of the lantern and dropping the
cash before picking it up. However the thing I regret the most is
inadvertently stealing from the shop without grabbing that magic lamp
first. Getting killed for robbing a shop is one thing, but to get
killed for robbing a shop of 16 zorkmids..?

